{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Carole "Kelly" Bishop (born February 28, 1944) is an American actress and dancer, best known for her roles as matriarch Emily Gilmore on the series "Gilmore Girls" and as Marjorie Houseman, the mother of Jennifer Grey's Frances "Baby" Houseman in the film "Dirty Dancing."","title":"Kelly Bishop"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Bishop created the role of Sheila in "A Chorus Line," for which she won a Tony Award for Best Performance by a Featured Actress in a Musical.","title":"Kelly Bishop"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She also starred as Fanny Flowers in the ABC Family short-lived comedy-drama series "Bunheads."","title":"Kelly Bishop"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sarah Charles Lewis (born August 2004) is an American actress.","title":"Sarah Charles Lewis"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She played Winnie Foster in the musical "Tuck Everlasting" on Broadway.","title":"Sarah Charles Lewis"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Wedding Bell Blues" is the thirteenth episode of the fifth season of the American comedy-drama series "Gilmore Girls" and the show's 100th episode overall.","title":"Wedding Bell Blues (Gilmore Girls)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Written and directed by series creator Amy Sherman-Palladino, the episode was originally broadcast on The WB in the United States on February 8, 2005.","title":"Wedding Bell Blues (Gilmore Girls)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The episode features the renewal of vows by Emily (Kelly Bishop) and Richard Gilmore (Edward Herrmann).","title":"Wedding Bell Blues (Gilmore Girls)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Their daughter Lorelai Gilmore (Lauren Graham) and their granddaughter Rory Gilmore (Alexis Bledel) serve as maid of honor and best man, respectively.","title":"Wedding Bell Blues (Gilmore Girls)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "Wedding Bell Blues" received positive reviews from television critics.","title":"Wedding Bell Blues (Gilmore Girls)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Paul Michael (August 15, 1926 – July 8, 2011) was an American actor.","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was a regular guest star on American television appearing in "Kojak", "Hill Street Blues", "Alias", "Gilmore Girls" and "Frasier".","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He played a cop in the Hollywood movie "Batman".","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He also played King Johnny Romano on "Dark Shadows".","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He was also in movies such as "Mask of the Red Death" and the TV movie "Where There's a Will".","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He was best known for his appearances on Broadway where he frequently played the title role in "Zorba the Greek", Tevia in "Fiddler on the Roof", and the barber in "The Man of La Mancha".","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" He danced in "Bells are Ringing" with Vivian Leigh.","title":"Paul Michael"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Kimberly Alexis Bledel ( ; ] ; born September 16, 1981) is an American actress and model.","title":"Alexis Bledel"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is known for her role as Rory Gilmore on the television series "Gilmore Girls" (2000–07), for which she received nominations for Satellite, Teen Choice and Young Artist Awards.","title":"Alexis Bledel"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Bledel made her feature film debut as Winnie Foster in "Tuck Everlasting" (2002), and has since appeared in "Sin City" (2005), "Post Grad" (2009), and as Lena Kaligaris in "The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants" film series.","title":"Alexis Bledel"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Bledel reprised her role as Rory Gilmore in the Netflix reunion miniseries "" (2016).","title":"Alexis Bledel"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" She won a Primetime Emmy Award for her work on the Hulu drama series "The Handmaid's Tale".","title":"Alexis Bledel"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Emily Gilmore is a fictional character who appears in the American comedy-drama television series "Gilmore Girls" (2000 – 2007) and its revival "" (2016) as the matriarch of the eponymous Gilmore family.","title":"Emily Gilmore"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Portrayed by actress Kelly Bishop, the character was created by series creator Amy Sherman-Palladino in order to add a more tragic element to the show's comedic nature.","title":"Emily Gilmore"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Emily has had a complicated relationship with her daughter Lorelai ever since the character runs away from home upon giving birth to her daughter Rory at age 16.","title":"Emily Gilmore"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" They remain estranged for several years until Lorelai asks her parents to help pay for Rory's schooling, to which Emily agrees on the condition that her daughter and granddaughter visit her and her husband Richard for dinner every Friday evening.","title":"Emily Gilmore"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Season 5
